From deac375bb11d9373aa7ac74ccc19183862b22d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:03:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?screen:=20slices=20=E2=80=94=20N=20source?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20rects=20onto=20perspective-correct=20destination=20quads,=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?live=20over=20AMCP=20APPLY?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HighAsCG WO-869 path (b). One <screen> consumer draws up to 64 slices of the
channel frame onto its window canvas (the configured window size; a resized
window scales them through the viewport). Slices replace the stretch/fill draw,
uncovered canvas stays black, slice order is z order. Without slices the old
draw path runs unchanged (byte-identical output verified).

- slice_geometry.h (no GL): slice {src x y w h, dst ul ur lr ll, opacity,
  feather l t r b, clip x y w h}; validation (finite, src w/h > 0, src clamped
  to the raster, convex non-degenerate quad of either winding so mirrored
  slices work); 6 vertices per slice with per-corner q from the diagonal
  intersection (as fill_texture_q_for_quad); half-texel source clamp so
  bilinear filtering never bleeds neighbouring pixels into a slice.
- Shaders: slice_mode uniform; q-divide of texture and quad-local coords,
  opacity x smoothstep feather ramps, premultiplied output. The non-slice
  branch is the old code.
- Draw: blending (GL_ONE, GL_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA) only when a slice has
  opacity < 1 or feather; clipped slices drawn alone under glScissor,
  unclipped ones batched; culling off.
- XML: <slices><slice><src/><dst/><opacity/><feather/><clip/></slice></slices>,
  logged; rejected with sbs-key, key-only, datavideo colour spaces.
- AMCP (via #1638 call()): APPLY <ch>-<600+device-1> SLICES SET <n> <21
  numbers per slice> | SLICES CLEAR (SET 0 = CLEAR). 202 on success, 403 on
  bad input (previous slices stay). The AMCP thread only validates and queues
  under a mutex; the render thread swaps at the top of its tick. No window
  recreation. A channel format change keeps the live set.
- INFO: screen/slices, screen/slice/<n>/src|dst|opacity|feather|clip,
  screen/dropped_frames, screen/presented_frames.
- casparcg.config reference block documents <slices> and the APPLY grammar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MxpJi7QVXYQA38FT76gLNj
